        <type>std::function&lt; void(int attempt, int attempts, const std::string &amp;reason, std::chrono::milliseconds wait)&gt;</type>
        <definition>std::function&lt;void(int attempt, int attempts, const std::string&amp; reason, std::chrono::milliseconds wait)&gt; AGRemapCore::FileDownload::onRetry</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>onRetry</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::FileDownload::onRetry</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Called just before each retry, if set -- with the attempt that just failed, how many
there are in total, why it failed, and how long #download is about to wait
:raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

A hook rather than a logger, because this class has no view and should not grow one:
:cpp:class:`RemapIniDownload` owns the :cpp:class:`BaseLogger` and wires this up in
its own ``fix``. Left unset a retry is silent, which is only right for a caller that
has nowhere to say it
</verbatim> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
